  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You have been given an integer KKK and four arrays AAA, BBB, CCC, and DDD with sizes SAS_ASA​, SBS_BSB​, SCS_CSC​ and SDS_DSD​ respectively.\n\nFollow the given steps:\n\n\nPick four indices xxx, yyy, zzz, and www from arrays AAA, BBB, CCC, and DDD respectively. Note that (1≤x≤SA)(1 \\le x \\le S_A)(1≤x≤SA​), (1≤y≤SB)(1 \\le y \\le S_B)(1≤y≤SB​), (1≤z≤SC)(1 \\le z \\le S_C)(1≤z≤SC​) and (1≤w≤SD)(1 \\le w \\le S_D)(1≤w≤SD​).\nThere are in total SA×SB×SC×SDS_A\\times S_B\\times S_C\\times S_DSA​×SB​×SC​×SD​ ways to do the above step. For each way, write down the value of (Ax+By)×(Cz+Dw)(A_x + B_y) \\times (C_z + D_w)(Ax​+By​)×(Cz​+Dw​) on a board.\nSort all the numbers written on the board in **non-decreasing** order.\nFind the KthK^{th}Kth element written on the board.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nFirst line contains five integers SAS_ASA​, SBS_BSB​, SCS_CSC​, SDS_DSD​ and KKK.\nThe second line contains SAS_ASA​ space-separated integers A1,A2,...,ASAA_1,A_2,...,A_{S_A}A1​,A2​,...,ASA​​ denoting the array AAA.\nThe third line contains SBS_BSB​ space-separated integers B1,B2,...,BSBB_1,B_2,...,B_{S_B}B1​,B2​,...,BSB​​ denoting the array BBB.\nThe fourth line contains SCS_CSC​ space-separated integers C1,C2,...,CSCC_1,C_2,...,C_{S_C}C1​,C2​,...,CSC​​ denoting the array CCC.\nThe fifth line contains SDS_DSD​ space-separated integers D1,D2,...,DSDD_1,D_2,...,D_{S_D}D1​,D2​,...,DSD​​ denoting the array DDD.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output the required number in a single line .",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤SA,SB,SC,SD≤3⋅1041 \\le S_A,S_B,S_C,S_D \\le 3 \\cdot 10^41≤SA​,SB​,SC​,SD​≤3⋅104",
      "1≤K≤SA×SB×SC×SD1 \\le K \\le S_A\\times S_B\\times S_C\\times S_D1≤K≤SA​×SB​×SC​×SD​",
      "0≤Ai,Bi,Ci,Di≤1050 \\le A_i, B_i, C_i, D_i \\le 10^50≤Ai​,Bi​,Ci​,Di​≤105"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
